# audit_p1 - L1 full sweep log (2026-10-18)

purpose: L1 full finite-triangle sweep of the pinned release
`review-01787854-v3` (commit `2e9976c4becbf97e31c56fe75fce07cdff5dd4ea`),
executed with the release's own `scripts/run_full_sweep.sh` - reserved as
optional by prereg section 8 ("run_full_sweep.sh optional (budget, section
8)"; "L1 full sweep optional only within these caps") and skipped in the
2026-10-18 L1 replay log (`reports/audit_p1_l1_replay_2026-10-18.log`).

decision (recorded BEFORE execution): the owner selected the optional
full sweep on 2026-10-18. No parameter, tolerance, selection, or cap is
changed in response to any result; the decision order is anchored by this
file's commit timestamp, and the machine log below records `repo_commit`
and the runner sha256 at run start.

budget cap (pre-registered): wall cap 6 h from `started_utc` recorded in
`REPLAY_METADATA.txt`. If exceeded the run is stopped and the item is
recorded UNRESOLVED-BUDGET (section-8 style); a cap change would be a new
dated decision, never a silent one. The cap is mechanically enforced by
`audit_p1/l1_sweep_watchdog.sh` (committed with this file), which stops
the run and appends the stop record to this log if the wall is reached.
(Measured anchors carried from prereg section 8: "barrier + tail lanes
add hours"; "full sweep = 3,149,013 lines". Review lanes on this machine
measured up to ~15 min per range.)

